ident isaiah safforki has  taken that to heart  uh and he's always wanted to  you know pay uh what uh he felt was an  invest  invasion of uh his nation so when abi  came to power in 2018  when he tried to bring peace between  ethiopia and eritrea  the tplf was never happy they they felt  uh  abby was creating a partnership with a  foreign nation that was  against the interests of tplf and that's  how the conflict begun  simon just uh very briefly what about  the the  uh humanitarian implications of this for  the region you mentioned as refugees  how serious is it  i mean so far 25 000 people official  number of 25 000  have moved to the sudan there are more  that haven't been accounted for  uh you know the people that have uh  moved to the sudan are telling us  that older people young children have  been left behind  the ngos have been pushed out of the  tigray region  they've been looted by the tpnf soldiers  they claimed so it's a disaster and it's  not just within ethiopia the conflict  it's not just way territory  but it will soon come to the european uh  nations  very soon samuel thank you very much  that was journalist samuel getachu  in addis ababa  thank you
 

